---
description: Flag every database stand-in with WAITING DATABASE so it is easy to find and wire later
alwaysApply: true
---

# Waiting on the database

There is no user/company database yet. Fixtures and `localStorage` stand in.

Whenever you persist, look up, or decide something that would normally hit a database (users, profiles, roles, companies, sessions, workspace, templates, requests, billing), mark it:

```
// WAITING DATABASE: <what the real API/table should own>
```

Use that exact token (`WAITING DATABASE`) so a later grep finds every site.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — silent fixture, easy to miss when wiring the API
localStorage.setItem("f2f.appearance", JSON.stringify(look));

// ✅ GOOD
// WAITING DATABASE: user.appearance — replace with the profile API
localStorage.setItem(`f2f.profile.${email}`, JSON.stringify(profile));
```

- Do not invent a second marker. Do not put stand-ins in unmarked helpers.
- Keep the note to one line: the resource and what replaces it.
- Login stays product-default (theme/accent/UI). Per-user prefs belong on that user's profile, never on a global key.
